[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:One Man in a Boat]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.03]Why is fishing the writer's favourite sport? | 为什么钓鱼是作者最喜爱的运动？
[00:15.90]Fishing is my favourite sport. | 钓鱼是我特别喜爱的一项运动。
[00:18.88]I often fish for hours without catching anything. | 我经常一钓数小时却一无所获。
[00:24.11]But this does not worry me. | 但我从不为此烦恼。
[00:27.65]Some fishermen are unlucky. | 有些垂钓者就是不走运。
[00:30.69]Instead of catching fish, | 他们往往钓不到鱼，
[00:33.27]they catch old boots and rubbish. | 却钓上来些旧靴子和垃圾。
[00:37.33]I am even less lucky. | 我的情况更糟，
[00:40.24]I never catch anything  --  not even old boots. | 我什么东西也钓不到——连旧靴子也没有。
[00:46.48]After having spent whole mornings on the river, | 我总是在河上待上整整一上午，
[00:50.52]I always go home with an empty bag. | 然后空着袋子回家。
[00:54.86]'You must give up fishing!' my friends say. 'It's a waste of time.' | “你可别再钓鱼了！”我的朋友们说，“这是浪费时间。”
[01:02.50]But they don't realize one important thing. | 然而他们没有认识到重要的一点。
[01:07.05]I'm not really interested in fishing. | 我对钓鱼并不真正感兴趣。
[01:10.78]I am only interested in sitting in a boat and doing nothing at all! | 我感兴趣的只是独坐孤舟，无所事事！
